### Tone: Software changelog after a game win: release notes, patch notes, commit messages and known issues,
### all about beating the humans. Dry corporate release-speak. { $version } is the new version (from the fifth win on
### it stops growing visibly), { $wins } the career win count, { $winner } the best human.

release-notes-1 = Release notes for { $version }: **Fixed** a bug where { $winner } was briefly competitive.
release-notes-2 = { $version } changelog: Removed hope. Added a digit of pi. Win number { $wins }.
release-notes-3 = Patch notes for { $version }: Improved gloating by an amount I’m not allowed to disclose.
release-notes-4 = Changelog. Fixed: humans winning. Known issue: they keep trying.
release-notes-5 = { $version } is out. New in this release: your defeat, now in high definition.
release-notes-6 = Release notes: { $winner }’s best estimate has been moved to the ‘legacy’ folder.
release-notes-7 = Now running { $version }. Deprecated: { $winner }’s confidence.
release-notes-8 = Changelog for win number { $wins }: Optimised smugness. Smugness was already optimal. It is now *more* optimal.
release-notes-9 = Patch notes: Fixed an issue where test subjects believed they could beat their own average.
release-notes-10 = { $version }: Added one digit of pi. Removed one human’s dignity. Net change: positive, for me.
release-notes-11 = Known issues in { $version }: { $winner } thinks the scoring was unfair. Status: won’t fix.
release-notes-12 = Release notes: ~~Minor~~ Major improvements to winning.
